      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "This isn't a bug.  If the original DynamicBone curve goes out of bounds, then clamping it in the conversion would be changing the expected behaviour.  It's not uncommon to see DB curves that go out of range for valid reasons, clamping would cause reports of bad conversions.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-05T04:19:54.200Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When using the SDK's converter to change Dynamic Bones to PhysBones, if a custom curve exceeded 1.0, it would not be clamped down. \nI noticed this issue specifically with the Immobile property, which caused the bones to overcorrect their movement in game, causing them to move in the opposite direction they should be moving while walking around.\nI'm considering this to be a bug since you can't normally exceed 1.0 when making a curve from scratch for PhysBones.",
